<card id="c" title="Zla Kolata and Prokletije: 300 Euros There and Back">
<do type="prev" label="Back"><prev/></do>
<p>While I was eating on a bench, the nearest kafana opened, and I went there for a coffee.</p>
<p>At that early hour, it was where the postmen gathered for coffee and a smoke. Every one of them in a yellow shirt, dark trousers and a brown bag. All of them no longer young, grey-haired, some with a decent bald patch. With every minute there were more of them, until there were about ten. It all looked like old friends getting together for coffee as a big group on a weekend morning.</p>
<p>After my coffee, I went back to the station and waited for the bus.</p>
<p>To my surprise, the bus, though small, was comfortable and had working air conditioning. There were few people, and for almost the whole ride I had both seats to myself.</p>
